WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.842
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:07.112 --> 00:09.073
[theme music playing]

3
00:46.694 --> 00:49.238
A LOVE OTHER THAN YOURS

4
00:49.405 --> 00:50.865
[theme music concludes]

5
00:52.616 --> 00:53.492
ALL PERSONS, LOCATIONS, RELIGIONS, INCIDENTS, AND ORGANIZATIONS IN THIS DRAMA

6
00:53.617 --> 00:54.451
ARE FICTITIOUS

7
00:54.577 --> 00:55.411
CHILD ACTORS HAVE FILMED SAFELY UNDER PARENTAL SUPERVISION

8
00:55.536 --> 00:56.370
SCENES INVOLVING ANIMALS WERE FILMED SAFELY WITH EXPERT ADVICE AND COOPERATION

9
00:57.872 --> 00:59.957
[Mi-do, over recording] Why would you go that far for me?

10
01:00.082 --> 01:01.166
[somber instrumental playing]

11
01:01.792 --> 01:02.835
[Mi-do] What do you want from me?

12
01:05.045 --> 01:06.171
[Tae-seung] I know one thing.

13
01:07.756 --> 01:08.966
It's not because of the settlement.

14
01:11.010 --> 01:13.053
-[door keypad beeps] -[kissing over recording]

15
01:14.430 --> 01:15.890
[panting]

16
01:38.579 --> 01:41.665
Wait, wait, Namgung, let me explain what happened.

17
01:46.378 --> 01:47.880
Let go of my arm, please.

18
02:01.477 --> 02:02.353
Explain?

19
02:03.938 --> 02:05.272
What's to explain?

20
02:08.817 --> 02:10.235
You said I shouldn't worry.

21
02:12.071 --> 02:13.155
That nothing happened.

22
02:15.908 --> 02:16.742
Hey, Mi-do.

23
02:17.660 --> 02:18.911
[breathes shakily]

24
02:27.503 --> 02:30.047
I honestly don't know what I was thinking that day.

25
02:32.257 --> 02:33.342
Everything I said.

26
02:34.635 --> 02:35.928
I didn't mean a word.

27
02:36.887 --> 02:38.347
It was the alcohol.

28
02:39.390 --> 02:42.226
I was so drunk that day, I wasn't even thinking straight.

29
02:42.351 --> 02:43.811
[Namgung] Will you cut the crap?

30
02:44.520 --> 02:46.855
I'm not in the mood to hear it right now.

31
02:54.905 --> 02:55.906
I'm sorry.

32
03:40.826 --> 03:42.327
[smashes]

33
03:51.587 --> 03:53.005
[somber instrumental music concludes]

34
03:53.130 --> 03:55.466
A LOVE OTHER THAN YOURS

35
03:55.591 --> 04:01.472
ARE WE ALLIES OR ENEMIES?

36
04:04.600 --> 04:06.393
HANGYEOL ORPHANAGE

37
04:06.560 --> 04:07.478
[director] Yes, Chairman.

38
04:08.145 --> 04:09.730
I heard Seong-hyeon won first place again.

39
04:10.439 --> 04:11.273
Congratulations.

40
04:11.398 --> 04:13.233
[mellow, muffled music playing over speakers]

41
04:13.358 --> 04:14.193
[director] Ah.

42
04:14.526 --> 04:16.570
I'll make sure to keep Tae-seung in line.

43
04:17.571 --> 04:20.574
I talked to Reporter Ko, so you don't need to worry about a thing.

44
04:21.492 --> 04:23.827
Yes. I'll be in touch with you shortly.

45
04:24.620 --> 04:25.537
[call drops]

46
04:34.797 --> 04:38.550
Tae-seung, what did I always tell you?

47
04:39.551 --> 04:41.178
You must share and give all the time.

48
04:43.472 --> 04:45.265
That makes you a good kid.

49
04:46.725 --> 04:47.684
You're wrong.

50
04:48.811 --> 04:49.853
I won't do it.

51
04:51.230 --> 04:53.148
I'll tip off another reporter.

52
04:54.358 --> 04:55.567
Wait, no.

53
04:56.735 --> 04:58.570
I'll even go to the news stations.

54
04:59.655 --> 05:01.073
From now on, I'll never…

55
05:02.908 --> 05:03.992
I swear it,

56
05:05.786 --> 05:07.287
take tests for someone else.

57
05:16.547 --> 05:18.048
-[music volume increases] -[door closes]

58
05:27.641 --> 05:28.767
[breathes shakily]

59
05:29.476 --> 05:30.602
-[mellow music concludes] -[gasps]

60
05:30.727 --> 05:32.563
[panting]

61
05:32.688 --> 05:34.356
[upbeat pop music playing over speakers]

62
05:43.448 --> 05:45.159
[upbeat pop music concludes]

63
05:55.836 --> 05:57.087
Mr. Han Tae-seung.

64
06:05.012 --> 06:07.973
[suspenseful music playing]

65
06:12.352 --> 06:14.980
[detective] This is Kim Jeong-hwan from Line Intercontinental.

66
06:15.105 --> 06:16.190
An acquaintance?

67
06:19.526 --> 06:25.657
[phone vibrating]

68
06:25.782 --> 06:27.618
INCOMING CALL

69
06:30.329 --> 06:32.247
[Jeong-hwan] Is this Attorney Han Tae-seung on the line?

70
06:32.372 --> 06:33.207
Who is this?

71
06:33.624 --> 06:34.750
[Jeong-hwan] I'm from Line Intercontinental.

72
06:35.209 --> 06:36.043
Kim Jeong-hwan.

73
06:36.752 --> 06:37.628
I'm calling with a tip.

74
06:38.337 --> 06:39.379
[grunts]

75
06:40.172 --> 06:43.217
You're about to fuck up your entire life for next to nothing.

76
06:43.342 --> 06:44.676
[music rises]

77
06:47.763 --> 06:49.348
[panting]

78
06:50.724 --> 06:51.558
[coughs weakly]

79
06:53.018 --> 06:55.103
[Tae-seung] Take the cash and go to that address.

80
06:55.354 --> 06:57.856
Don't pick up any calls until you hear from me.

81
07:01.443 --> 07:02.361
This isn't for me.

82
07:03.946 --> 07:04.780
It's for you.

83
07:06.406 --> 07:10.285
If you want to live and keep this money, do as I say.

84
07:13.080 --> 07:14.039
Oh…

85
07:15.123 --> 07:16.541
I thought it was just a joke.

86
07:18.752 --> 07:20.462
So he was a researcher after all.

87
07:24.174 --> 07:26.551
[detective] This is Kim Jeong-hwan's last known location.

88
07:27.052 --> 07:29.429
Coincidentally, it's an alley near Jaekang Law Firm.

89
07:30.889 --> 07:32.933
Can you confirm where you were at that time, sir?

90
07:33.725 --> 07:35.269
The day of Seoul's first snow?

91
07:36.561 --> 07:38.021
I think…

92
07:40.107 --> 07:42.192
Jaekang Law Firm's security was hacked.

93
07:42.317 --> 07:44.152
The security cameras weren't available to check.

94
07:46.697 --> 07:49.908
Can anyone verify your whereabouts after 10:00 p.m.?

95
08:01.962 --> 08:02.963
No, sir.

96
08:03.547 --> 08:04.381
Nobody can.

97
08:04.506 --> 08:05.590
[suspenseful music concludes]

98
08:06.717 --> 08:10.554
[Ju-hyeok] You honestly didn't see Kim Jeong-hwan?

99
08:11.138 --> 08:13.807
It's a bit shocking you didn't see a guy walking into a building.

100
08:14.516 --> 08:16.893
That was before I knew he ran off with internal data.

101
08:18.603 --> 08:23.525
I figured Line was playing dirty tricks before the trial, so I ignored it.

102
08:26.028 --> 08:27.362
-[sighs] -[chopsticks clatter]

103
08:30.574 --> 08:33.410
No matter what happens, we have to find that data

104
08:33.535 --> 08:35.037
and Kim Jeong-hwan before Jisang does.

105
08:36.038 --> 08:36.955
Don't worry about it.

106
08:38.081 --> 08:39.708
I'm looking into every connection,

107
08:40.751 --> 08:43.170
including trying to track down his old sweetheart.

108
08:43.795 --> 08:44.796
[chuckles softly]

109
08:46.631 --> 08:47.924
[laughs]

110
08:48.759 --> 08:49.801
Then I'm good.

111
08:49.926 --> 08:51.553
And don't worry about the police.

112
08:52.262 --> 08:53.555
The higher-ups will sort it out.

113
08:53.680 --> 08:56.767
[phone vibrating]

114
08:59.269 --> 09:00.270
Attorney Lee.

115
09:00.395 --> 09:01.396
[slurps]

116
09:06.193 --> 09:07.986
What the hell is taking so long?

117
09:09.696 --> 09:10.530
What?

118
09:12.824 --> 09:13.658
An hour.

119
09:17.621 --> 09:18.914
[Tae-seung] Living room console.

120
09:20.082 --> 09:22.167
Inside it, there's a silver safe.

121
09:23.126 --> 09:24.211
[tense music playing]

122
09:24.336 --> 09:28.382
But what you're looking for won't be in there, so…

123
09:29.591 --> 09:30.550
[chuckles]

124
09:34.137 --> 09:35.180
You hear that?

125
09:36.390 --> 09:37.391
Bring it here now.

126
09:44.981 --> 09:46.274
Since when did you know?

127
09:49.528 --> 09:52.364
I found out on the 3rd that Line was raided by the FSS.

128
09:53.865 --> 09:56.827
And yesterday I found a Malaysian account I didn't know existed.

129
09:56.952 --> 09:58.912
There was some guy who deposited money into it.

130
09:59.037 --> 10:00.914
It was Director Bang from the Line.

131
10:03.583 --> 10:04.584
Forty-five minutes ago?

132
10:07.671 --> 10:10.090
Things got complicated with Line's succession issue.

133
10:11.049 --> 10:14.219
If Assemblyman Shin's airport project fails, it'll get worse.

134
10:15.220 --> 10:16.972
We'll handle the settlement outside of court.

135
10:18.056 --> 10:19.599
Think of it as a few years off.

136
10:19.724 --> 10:21.059
Cooperate with them.

137
10:25.480 --> 10:26.314
What if I say no?

138
10:30.652 --> 10:31.903
[music rises]

139
10:32.028 --> 10:33.113
I'll assume you have…

140
10:35.615 --> 10:36.741
Kim Jeong-hwan's data.

141
10:39.411 --> 10:40.787
You think that's all I got?

142
10:42.622 --> 10:44.833
For the past five years, I've been working under you.

143
10:52.048 --> 10:53.008
You got one week.

144
10:54.426 --> 10:56.678
Handle my police investigation first.

145
10:57.971 --> 11:02.642
Otherwise, your father-in-law will be the first to be investigated.

146
11:10.025 --> 11:11.610
[tense music crescendos, concludes]

147
11:12.277 --> 11:13.111
[Wan-do] Did they fight?

148
11:13.653 --> 11:15.947
[Yeong-do] Still, why would he ghost us for days like this?

149
11:16.072 --> 11:17.491
[door keypad beeping]

150
11:18.950 --> 11:19.784
Namgung!

151
11:20.994 --> 11:22.204
Hey, you in there?

152
11:33.590 --> 11:34.549
Mi-do.

153
11:35.383 --> 11:36.218
What?

154
11:39.179 --> 11:40.013
Mi-do.

155
11:47.979 --> 11:49.523
[gentle, somber music playing]

156
11:58.573 --> 12:01.826
CHAT YEONG-DO

157
12:01.993 --> 12:03.578
[Yeong-do] Hey Namgung, good job.

158
12:03.828 --> 12:06.748
I don't know what's going on, but Mi-do looks completely wrecked

159
12:06.873 --> 12:07.707
and is really sorry.

160
12:09.376 --> 12:12.003
Anyway, Namgung, is it this Friday or next week?

161
12:12.754 --> 12:14.506
The pickup for Mom's blood pressure meds.

162
12:16.508 --> 12:17.926
[Wan-do] Nothing's wrong, right?

163
12:18.218 --> 12:19.678
Where are you staying right now?

164
12:21.054 --> 12:22.973
The card reader broke again.

165
12:23.306 --> 12:24.975
Got the repair center number?

166
12:25.100 --> 12:26.142
[phone vibrating]

167
12:26.268 --> 12:27.811
MIDORI

168
12:33.066 --> 12:35.652
[phone continues vibrating]

169
13:00.343 --> 13:02.178
[gentle, somber music concludes]

170
13:11.980 --> 13:12.939
Come back home.

171
13:13.648 --> 13:14.774
I'll move out.

172
13:15.984 --> 13:17.277
You can't sleep well anywhere else.

173
13:19.487 --> 13:20.655
Let me ask you this.

174
13:23.825 --> 13:25.744
Am I the reason you're a film director?

175
13:31.666 --> 13:32.959
It's not like that, Namgung.

176
13:34.210 --> 13:35.045
It's not.

177
13:36.796 --> 13:38.340
Then what was that scumbag saying?

178
13:39.966 --> 13:43.428
He said you wanted to run away, but you were too ashamed to tell me.

179
13:45.430 --> 13:46.765
I was just so exhausted.

180
13:47.724 --> 13:49.142
It was the heat of the moment.

181
13:50.101 --> 13:51.186
[sorrowful music playing]

182
13:51.936 --> 13:55.273
Honestly, I should have just given up after all this failure.

183
13:56.941 --> 13:58.068
But that was too hard.

184
13:59.486 --> 14:00.820
You were the excuse.

185
14:03.657 --> 14:05.116
Actually, Namgung,

186
14:06.242 --> 14:08.953
while shooting this film, I realized something.

187
14:12.374 --> 14:16.419
My skill set is completely pathetic.

188
14:18.254 --> 14:21.383
I truly don't have what it takes to shoot a film of this scale.

189
14:22.801 --> 14:23.885
And I'm not lying.

190
14:24.803 --> 14:25.637
I swear.

191
14:27.597 --> 14:30.266
I'm not as good a director as you think I am.

192
14:31.476 --> 14:34.521
It's not because of bad luck or lack of opportunity.

193
14:36.189 --> 14:37.607
I just have no talent.

194
14:39.609 --> 14:40.985
[exhales softly]

195
14:45.323 --> 14:46.700
I'm terrible, aren't I?

196
14:48.493 --> 14:49.828
I surely let you down.

197
14:50.578 --> 14:52.580
You really are some piece of work.

198
14:54.207 --> 14:55.917
Why are you telling me this now?

199
14:57.127 --> 14:57.961
I'm not an idiot.

200
14:58.086 --> 15:00.630
I know you want me to pity you and let this slide.

201
15:00.922 --> 15:01.756
Why?

202
15:02.507 --> 15:04.050
To you, am I just some dumb sucker

203
15:04.175 --> 15:07.095
who believes it's the end of the world if you're hurt, huh?

204
15:07.846 --> 15:09.264
You're using me right now.

205
15:10.098 --> 15:11.474
You're using your misery against me

206
15:11.725 --> 15:13.643
because you know I fucking care about you!

207
15:16.646 --> 15:18.356
Mm-hmm. You're right.

208
15:19.983 --> 15:21.025
I'm using you.

209
15:22.152 --> 15:24.112
So I'm just asking you one more time.

210
15:26.364 --> 15:28.032
Please let everything go again.

211
15:36.374 --> 15:37.584
[Namgung] No, I can't.

212
15:39.127 --> 15:40.503
I can't see you the same.

213
15:41.254 --> 15:43.465
And I've thought about it a hundred times over.

214
15:45.008 --> 15:46.634
[music rises]

215
15:49.095 --> 15:50.638
We need to rethink this wedding.

216
15:54.017 --> 15:55.435
So please leave if you're done.

217
16:04.944 --> 16:06.196
[sorrowful music concludes]

218
16:09.199 --> 16:11.576
You shouldn't get too comfortable here.

219
16:13.286 --> 16:15.246
Only until you're completely healed.

220
16:18.541 --> 16:19.667
[meows]

221
16:19.793 --> 16:20.960
[hisses]

222
16:21.336 --> 16:22.879
Hey, don't give me that cute look!

223
16:23.630 --> 16:24.464
Hmm.

224
16:25.131 --> 16:28.343
You're a living thing, so I'd have to take care of you for life,

225
16:28.468 --> 16:30.261
and I don't think I can handle that.

226
16:32.347 --> 16:34.432
I'm looking for a good adopter, so just wait.

227
16:40.355 --> 16:42.690
I'm thinking of one perfect adopter.

228
16:43.441 --> 16:44.442
[meows]

229
16:44.943 --> 16:46.402
[perky music playing]

230
16:47.070 --> 16:49.614
Bambi, it's someone you know too,

231
16:49.739 --> 16:52.283
and he has some experience as a cat dad.

232
16:52.826 --> 16:55.995
And I bet you'd prefer someone you know over a total stranger, right?

233
16:56.746 --> 17:00.333
Hmm. I already asked him, and sent your picture just in case.

234
17:04.629 --> 17:06.923
Oh, right, he read it and didn't reply.

235
17:11.719 --> 17:14.305
Bambi, let me show you, okay?

236
17:16.224 --> 17:17.433
Hey, take a look.

237
17:18.893 --> 17:20.395
This is too much, right?

238
17:21.896 --> 17:24.649
Sure, he's been going through a rough patch lately.

239
17:26.150 --> 17:29.404
But even though I clearly sent this message

240
17:29.529 --> 17:31.531
because I was worried about him,

241
17:31.656 --> 17:33.283
ghosting is rude.

242
17:33.992 --> 17:35.702
Look, I wrote this huge text.

243
17:36.578 --> 17:37.871
And you're so cute.

244
17:38.663 --> 17:39.873
[meows]

245
17:43.167 --> 17:44.377
Yeah. Hmm.

246
17:45.211 --> 17:46.880
He can leave me on read.

247
17:47.422 --> 17:48.381
Mm-hmm.

248
17:48.840 --> 17:49.757
I don't matter.

249
17:52.969 --> 17:54.095
[sighs]

250
17:54.512 --> 17:55.430
TF TEAM 3 NAMGUNG HO

251
17:55.555 --> 17:56.472
[Su-a] Huh?

252
17:57.765 --> 17:58.808
Why is…

253
18:00.310 --> 18:01.352
[gasps]

254
18:01.936 --> 18:03.271
-[perky music concludes] -[screams]

255
18:03.396 --> 18:04.355
[gasps]

256
18:05.899 --> 18:07.525
Why is that picture there? Huh?

257
18:07.650 --> 18:13.031
HUNMIN CONFECTIONERY

258
18:23.958 --> 18:25.501
[intriguing music playing]

259
18:30.673 --> 18:33.426
[GPS tracker beeping]

260
18:36.387 --> 18:38.264
HUNMIN CONFECTIONERY

261
18:40.808 --> 18:42.727
[researcher] I made the sugar adjustment you requested.

262
18:43.770 --> 18:46.773
Surface moisture is 0.8 lower than the fourth batch.

263
18:48.691 --> 18:50.610
I let it cool so it won't be hot.

264
18:54.155 --> 18:55.073
Sir?

265
18:55.740 --> 18:56.741
Mr. Namgung.

266
18:57.325 --> 18:58.576
Oh, right.

267
19:00.787 --> 19:03.247
[munching]

268
19:14.884 --> 19:17.929
[researcher] We followed the recipe, but they have a weird aftertaste, right?

269
19:19.305 --> 19:20.306
These sweet potatoes.

270
19:21.265 --> 19:23.226
Usually the farm delivers a small batch to us,

271
19:23.351 --> 19:26.646
but I had to go to the Cheonan factory, so I grabbed a few from there.

272
19:27.397 --> 19:30.149
The factory manager found out later and threw a huge fit.

273
19:31.192 --> 19:32.318
Any sweet potatoes left?

274
19:32.944 --> 19:34.445
There's no way you could have used them all.

275
19:34.570 --> 19:37.532
Uh… well, Mr. Namgung took them this morning.

276
19:38.324 --> 19:39.242
Huh?

277
19:43.663 --> 19:44.956
The left side is slippery.

278
19:45.957 --> 19:47.250
[intriguing music concludes]

279
19:48.334 --> 19:49.961
[Su-a] You knew when you took them, right?

280
19:50.837 --> 19:52.046
Where are the sweet potatoes?

281
19:53.589 --> 19:55.383
And why exactly should I tell you?

282
19:57.051 --> 19:58.970
Those are imported. I know for sure.

283
19:59.429 --> 20:01.222
Imports have different pesticide levels.

284
20:01.347 --> 20:03.641
Testing them will give us solid evidence.

285
20:04.767 --> 20:06.728
The Bread Pie Mass Rebate incident.

286
20:08.312 --> 20:09.147
Heard of it?

287
20:09.939 --> 20:10.773
Yeah.

288
20:11.691 --> 20:12.900
It's a famous case.

289
20:13.026 --> 20:14.777
Manager Eom was part of that team.

290
20:15.987 --> 20:18.281
People think that they were caught in an audit and fired.

291
20:18.406 --> 20:19.240
It wasn't like that.

292
20:19.866 --> 20:20.908
They were demoted.

293
20:21.451 --> 20:22.577
It was retaliation.

294
20:23.161 --> 20:24.704
They were about to blow the whistle.

295
20:26.456 --> 20:27.540
Except for Manager Eom,

296
20:27.665 --> 20:32.086
the rest of the team, they all quit within a calendar year.

297
20:33.129 --> 20:34.547
He couldn't afford to quit.

298
20:36.924 --> 20:38.509
His oldest plays the piano.

299
20:39.969 --> 20:41.471
She was way too good at it.

300
20:42.472 --> 20:45.558
[classical piano music playing over phone speakers]

301
20:50.104 --> 20:52.815
[Namgung] They might have demoted him or transferred him

302
20:52.940 --> 20:54.609
to a plant in the middle of damn nowhere.

303
20:54.734 --> 20:57.403
He'd be shunned by the team and denied promotions.

304
20:58.029 --> 20:59.238
Who could endure all that?

305
20:59.739 --> 21:03.826
Manager Eom said he'd have quit if his daughter were just smart.

306
21:04.452 --> 21:07.789
Unfortunately, she's a complete prodigy.

307
21:08.998 --> 21:09.999
You're trying to scare me.

308
21:10.124 --> 21:11.209
That's why you say that.

309
21:11.334 --> 21:13.086
[Namgung] I forgot the most important part.

310
21:13.503 --> 21:16.005
They even went and dug up his family history.

311
21:16.923 --> 21:17.924
[tender music playing]

312
21:18.049 --> 21:21.677
His wife was the victim of a crime severe enough to make the news.

313
21:24.138 --> 21:25.765
They posted it on the company chat.

314
21:38.111 --> 21:40.988
This issue might be a little more complex than you realize.

315
21:44.450 --> 21:45.785
I'm prepared for that.

316
21:46.452 --> 21:48.496
You're managing everything just fine.

317
21:49.372 --> 21:50.665
I can do that too.

318
21:52.291 --> 21:53.209
[scoffs]

319
21:53.543 --> 21:54.627
I don't think so.

320
21:57.505 --> 21:58.756
I'm actually struggling.

321
22:02.135 --> 22:03.511
Even more than you think.

322
22:08.141 --> 22:10.143
-Have a good night. -You too. Have a good night.

323
22:12.603 --> 22:13.688
Oh, Su-a.

324
22:13.813 --> 22:15.481
Your report got rejected again?

325
22:15.898 --> 22:16.983
Let's just head out.

326
22:17.108 --> 22:18.317
I'll stay a bit longer.

327
22:18.442 --> 22:19.527
You can go ahead.

328
22:19.652 --> 22:21.237
[Sang-hun] Oh, really? Okay.

329
22:22.280 --> 22:23.656
Well, actually, I was going

330
22:23.781 --> 22:26.033
to suggest we go cheer up Assistant Manager Gung.

331
22:26.742 --> 22:27.577
Huh?

332
22:30.454 --> 22:32.748
[upbeat pop song playing faintly over speakers]

333
22:49.265 --> 22:51.851
-Careful, be careful. -[Sang-hun] Whoa, this is… [groans]

334
22:51.976 --> 22:53.436
Okay, I got it.

335
22:53.978 --> 22:55.146
[sighs] Whoa.

336
22:55.730 --> 22:56.814
[exhales wearily]

337
22:58.024 --> 22:59.275
Wow, uh…

338
22:59.901 --> 23:01.152
Jeez, Mr. Namgung.

339
23:01.777 --> 23:03.821
You must be really having a hard time.

340
23:04.280 --> 23:05.281
[phone vibrating]

341
23:05.406 --> 23:07.325
[Sang-hun] Yes, hello? Is this the driver?

342
23:07.950 --> 23:08.784
No!

343
23:08.910 --> 23:11.412
We're at exit four, not exit three.

344
23:12.246 --> 23:13.581
It's on the opposite side.

345
23:13.706 --> 23:14.540
No!

346
23:15.249 --> 23:16.792
Not exit three. Wait.

347
23:25.092 --> 23:26.552
[exhales deeply]

348
23:34.143 --> 23:37.396
Mr. Namgung, are you actually that drunk?

349
23:42.193 --> 23:45.488
What you told me was a lie, right?

350
23:45.613 --> 23:47.198
To make me throw in the towel.

351
23:53.287 --> 23:54.413
Is this an act too?

352
23:55.164 --> 23:57.375
One bottle of soju can't make you this drunk.

353
24:00.962 --> 24:02.380
Are you lying about this too?

354
24:09.595 --> 24:12.890
Okay then, since you're really drunk,

355
24:15.184 --> 24:16.644
can I tell you something?

356
24:19.188 --> 24:21.107
Because I might never get another chance.

357
24:29.282 --> 24:30.574
Mr. Namgung,

358
24:34.036 --> 24:34.870
I really…

359
24:37.164 --> 24:38.082
I like…

360
24:38.207 --> 24:39.500
[grunts softly]

361
24:42.461 --> 24:43.546
[bouncy music playing]

362
24:43.671 --> 24:44.839
And the sweet potatoes.

363
24:46.757 --> 24:48.134
Have you thrown them away?

364
24:48.259 --> 24:49.719
No, you wouldn't dare, right?

365
24:52.346 --> 24:53.306
[sleepily] They're gone.

366
24:53.431 --> 24:54.265
What?!

367
24:54.390 --> 24:55.224
You did?

368
24:59.770 --> 25:00.771
Okay.

369
25:00.896 --> 25:02.898
Where did you throw them away, huh?

370
25:04.025 --> 25:06.193
[mumbling] Maybe Route 6…

371
25:06.319 --> 25:07.153
Come again?

372
25:09.322 --> 25:11.157
Maybe Route 6.

373
25:11.282 --> 25:12.783
Maybe-- Maybe Route 6?

374
25:12.908 --> 25:13.993
Route 6.

375
25:14.660 --> 25:15.494
Ah!

376
25:15.619 --> 25:17.288
From Incheon Center to Seoul!

377
25:17.413 --> 25:22.168
[mumbling] Keep your joints healthy

378
25:22.293 --> 25:25.087
until you're 80.

379
25:25.796 --> 25:26.839
Knee slap.

380
25:26.964 --> 25:27.798
What?

381
25:28.716 --> 25:32.887
[mumbling] Keep your 20-year-old joints healthy until you're 80.

382
25:33.637 --> 25:35.139
Knee slap.

383
25:35.264 --> 25:37.683
You threw them at the "20-year-old joints" sign?

384
25:37.808 --> 25:39.602
Knee slap, knee slap… Knee slap!

385
25:40.519 --> 25:41.437
Of course.

386
25:42.063 --> 25:43.773
By the Dongbo Pharma billboard.

387
25:43.898 --> 25:45.191
There's a field and a drain.

388
25:45.316 --> 25:46.275
Am I right?

389
25:46.734 --> 25:48.736
Hey, tell me, you dumped them there?

390
25:48.861 --> 25:50.029
[bouncy music concludes]

391
25:58.329 --> 26:00.247
[soft music playing]

392
26:08.923 --> 26:10.341
[Namgung groans softly]

393
26:14.887 --> 26:15.888
Mi-do…

394
26:21.185 --> 26:22.645
Mi-do…

395
26:38.035 --> 26:39.161
[soft music concludes]

396
26:45.292 --> 26:46.419
[bright music playing over speakers]

397
26:46.544 --> 26:48.170
Did she skip today again?

398
26:49.797 --> 26:50.756
[groans in pain]

399
26:52.216 --> 26:54.677
Did she really quit directing or what?

400
26:54.802 --> 26:55.719
Huh…

401
26:56.178 --> 26:57.346
[groans]

402
26:57.471 --> 26:58.931
Is there a way to see inside?

403
27:10.109 --> 27:11.110
[clears throat]

404
27:11.235 --> 27:14.655
[phone vibrating]

405
27:30.212 --> 27:32.465
Hey, Tae-seung, you're late.

406
27:32.923 --> 27:34.049
We started without you.

407
27:38.804 --> 27:39.889
[subdued music playing]

408
27:44.685 --> 27:46.729
Could you tell me what is going on?

409
27:46.854 --> 27:48.314
[Ju-hyeok] What does it look like?

410
27:49.565 --> 27:51.525
I specifically begged Director Lee.

411
27:52.276 --> 27:54.570
I asked her to help you out, just this once.

412
27:57.448 --> 27:58.282
Sit down.

413
28:05.748 --> 28:09.335
It seems Tae-seung hid it because he was afraid of causing you trouble.

414
28:10.419 --> 28:12.087
He's in a tough spot right now.

415
28:12.755 --> 28:15.758
We are desperate, so your testimony would come in handy.

416
28:16.800 --> 28:18.469
[music rises]

417
28:18.594 --> 28:20.638
[Ju-hyeok] I suppose you have a lot to talk about.

418
28:21.180 --> 28:22.556
I'll be on my way now.

419
28:24.850 --> 28:25.893
I have a big trial.

420
28:43.661 --> 28:46.163
I have no idea what Seo told you before I arrived, but--

421
28:46.288 --> 28:47.331
I'm not testifying.

422
28:48.707 --> 28:50.209
I don't buy everything he says,

423
28:50.334 --> 28:53.462
but I don't want to be involved with you anymore.

424
28:55.381 --> 28:57.716
I wouldn't have come if I'd known you'd be here.

425
28:58.842 --> 28:59.843
So I'm leaving now.

426
29:06.100 --> 29:07.268
[subdued music concludes]

427
29:11.522 --> 29:12.815
[panting]

428
29:13.857 --> 29:16.485
If you don't testify, my career as a lawyer is over.

429
29:17.486 --> 29:18.612
You still won't do it?

430
29:20.322 --> 29:22.241
You got the skills, Tae-seung.

431
29:23.200 --> 29:25.160
I know you're very, very resourceful.

432
29:25.286 --> 29:26.328
You'll find a way out.

433
29:26.453 --> 29:27.413
No, I'm serious.

434
29:28.289 --> 29:30.624
If you don't testify, my whole life is screwed.

435
29:30.749 --> 29:32.167
You really won't testify?

436
29:37.381 --> 29:38.257
No.

437
29:43.262 --> 29:44.096
[Tae-seung] Wow.

438
29:45.347 --> 29:46.181
Well, that's harsh.

439
29:47.558 --> 29:48.642
I'm not being harsh.

440
29:49.768 --> 29:52.771
You fell into this trap because you work for a man like him.

441
29:54.064 --> 29:56.734
Just grit your teeth and happily carry on.

442
29:57.276 --> 29:58.110
You can do it.

443
29:59.153 --> 30:00.195
A trap?

444
30:06.410 --> 30:07.244
A trap.

445
30:08.454 --> 30:09.872
This wasn't a trap at all.

446
30:12.833 --> 30:14.460
[grave music playing]

447
30:15.169 --> 30:16.295
I threw that trial.

448
30:18.589 --> 30:19.548
But I lost on purpose.

449
30:23.719 --> 30:24.970
And that whistleblower?

450
30:26.263 --> 30:27.806
I just met him that day, you know?

451
30:30.851 --> 30:31.810
I don't buy it.

452
30:31.935 --> 30:32.936
That was the day…

453
30:33.062 --> 30:36.357
While you were sleeping, I went there and handled the issue.

454
30:37.399 --> 30:38.525
Ten minutes.

455
30:39.193 --> 30:40.361
That's all it took.

456
30:41.487 --> 30:43.113
I work at a pretty fast pace.

457
30:48.202 --> 30:49.203
Fine, Director Lee.

458
30:52.247 --> 30:53.207
Keep treating me like this.

459
30:54.958 --> 30:56.877
Keep ignoring me like I'm invisible.

460
30:59.546 --> 31:02.007
If I lose my mind and call, don't answer.

461
31:02.132 --> 31:03.342
Even if I show up.

462
31:06.637 --> 31:07.721
Ignore me.

463
31:10.432 --> 31:11.850
Same goes for Seo Ju-hyeok.

464
31:14.478 --> 31:17.564
This better be the last time you come running at his call and command.

465
31:18.691 --> 31:19.817
Or else…

466
31:23.320 --> 31:25.656
I'll make sure you won't have a place to run.

467
31:31.036 --> 31:33.080
[music rises]

468
31:42.047 --> 31:43.006
What happened?!

469
31:43.132 --> 31:45.134
You said you wiped everything, the video and the logs.

470
31:45.259 --> 31:46.677
[Hae-ju] Yeah, I wiped everything.

471
31:46.802 --> 31:48.345
Then how does Seo Ju-hyeok know Mi-do?

472
31:49.263 --> 31:51.265
How the hell does he know?

473
31:51.390 --> 31:53.642
[Hae-ju] Oh, uh, because I gave them to him.

474
31:55.310 --> 31:58.397
I'm sorry, but Seo's offer was just too good to pass up.

475
31:59.064 --> 32:00.357
But I didn't give up the whistleblower.

476
32:00.816 --> 32:03.485
That's my final act of loyalty after three years.

477
32:04.111 --> 32:05.154
Best of luck to you.

478
32:12.828 --> 32:14.413
[breathes deeply]

479
32:14.538 --> 32:15.414
[grave music concludes]

480
32:18.417 --> 32:19.668
[tires screech]

481
32:33.807 --> 32:35.225
Everything you said was true?

482
32:38.395 --> 32:39.229
Answer me.

483
32:39.688 --> 32:40.647
Is it all true?

484
32:42.357 --> 32:43.442
[breathing heavily]

485
32:43.984 --> 32:48.822
[car horn honking]

486
33:02.753 --> 33:04.171
[Mi-do] You lost the trial on purpose,

487
33:04.922 --> 33:08.550
and also decided to put that so-called whistleblower up to it?

488
33:09.718 --> 33:10.552
So what?

489
33:11.345 --> 33:12.513
Are you going to the cops to snitch?

490
33:13.013 --> 33:13.847
Just answer me!

491
33:14.723 --> 33:15.557
Am I right?

492
33:15.682 --> 33:17.351
Yeah, you're right.

493
33:17.476 --> 33:18.435
What's up with you?

494
33:18.685 --> 33:19.937
[exhales sharply]

495
33:20.270 --> 33:21.855
Thought you knew I was a piece of shit.

496
33:21.980 --> 33:23.190
Oh yes, I knew.

497
33:23.774 --> 33:26.652
But I'd hope you'd be a plastic can that takes ten years to rot.

498
33:27.486 --> 33:28.821
But I see now that you're not.

499
33:29.488 --> 33:31.031
You really are a tin can shit!

500
33:31.532 --> 33:34.451
A tin can shit that takes over 200 years to decompose!

501
33:35.869 --> 33:37.746
So what is it you want me to do, hush?

502
33:38.747 --> 33:40.415
Who cares if I'm a tin can piece of shit?

503
33:41.333 --> 33:43.210
I already told you I'd never come to see you again.

504
33:44.336 --> 33:46.421
I already told you I'd get out of your fucking life!

505
33:46.547 --> 33:48.257
So what the hell is your issue right now, huh?

506
33:48.382 --> 33:51.343
I'm losing it because you're even more pathetic than I thought!

507
33:54.930 --> 33:58.684
It completely pisses me off that I hurt the person I love most

508
33:58.809 --> 34:00.477
over a pathetic bastard like you.

509
34:01.061 --> 34:02.896
Shut the fuck up.

510
34:03.313 --> 34:04.773
I'm a fucking crazy bitch.

511
34:05.190 --> 34:08.569
I'm a crazy bitch for having feelings for this bastard.

512
34:10.028 --> 34:12.447
-[tender music playing] -[Mi-do sobbing softly]

513
34:14.533 --> 34:15.951
[tires screech]

514
34:19.288 --> 34:22.457
[sobbing softly]

515
34:25.961 --> 34:27.588
[music swells]

516
34:44.229 --> 34:49.818
[car horns honking]

517
34:54.448 --> 34:55.282
Mi-do.

518
34:55.407 --> 34:57.659
[tires screeching]

519
34:59.912 --> 35:02.748
[tires screech]

520
35:11.924 --> 35:13.592
[music falls]

521
35:13.717 --> 35:14.801
[winces]

522
35:29.524 --> 35:31.443
Mi-do. Mi-do!

523
35:42.037 --> 35:43.121
[tender music concludes]

524
35:43.246 --> 35:44.873
[indistinct chatter over PA]

525
35:44.998 --> 35:45.832
Are you awake?

526
35:50.087 --> 35:50.921
Mi-do.

527
35:51.046 --> 35:52.089
Do you feel okay?

528
35:55.509 --> 35:56.802
[grunts softly]

529
36:02.099 --> 36:03.308
How did I get here?

530
36:04.267 --> 36:05.102
Did you forget?

531
36:10.732 --> 36:11.817
There was a crash.

532
36:13.151 --> 36:14.069
[exhales deeply]

533
36:14.736 --> 36:15.696
I'll get a doctor.

534
36:15.821 --> 36:17.114
No, wait. I'm fine.

535
36:17.239 --> 36:18.824
You're not fine. Don't say that.

536
36:19.533 --> 36:21.034
I know I can be a bit impulsive.

537
36:22.828 --> 36:23.996
I may have startled you.

538
36:24.121 --> 36:25.163
I'm sorry.

539
36:27.916 --> 36:28.959
Your brother is on his way.

540
36:30.794 --> 36:33.338
A guardian is required for you to take the tests.

541
36:34.047 --> 36:36.299
He happened to call, so I explained the whole situation.

542
36:38.093 --> 36:39.678
He should be here by now.

543
36:39.803 --> 36:40.762
Come with me.

544
36:41.805 --> 36:42.931
Hey, what?

545
36:44.266 --> 36:47.644
I… I didn't want to answer the phone either.

546
36:48.186 --> 36:51.231
The thing is, my car hit you, so I'm the one at fault here.

547
36:52.065 --> 36:53.692
Leaving now would cause a lot of issues.

548
36:54.026 --> 36:56.236
You're already on the wrong side of the law.

549
36:56.361 --> 36:58.238
One more charge won't make a difference.

550
36:59.197 --> 37:00.240
Uh… what?

551
37:00.866 --> 37:03.452
I'm hurt and tired, so just keep walking, okay?

552
37:03.869 --> 37:04.703
Okay.

553
37:04.828 --> 37:05.912
Okay, I'll go.

554
37:06.371 --> 37:07.414
I said I'm coming.

555
37:07.539 --> 37:09.374
Hey, you need to be careful right now.

556
37:10.667 --> 37:11.501
Are you in pain?

557
37:12.127 --> 37:14.629
Do you feel pain anywhere else?

558
37:15.130 --> 37:15.964
What about you?

559
37:19.885 --> 37:20.844
[heartfelt music playing]

560
37:20.969 --> 37:22.179
Did you get hurt in the crash?

561
37:23.847 --> 37:25.474
I know you're terrified of needles.

562
37:26.850 --> 37:28.060
You're not hurt, are you?

563
37:34.232 --> 37:35.567
[Yeong-do] You piece of shit!

564
37:35.692 --> 37:36.902
[Tae-seung] Who the hell are you?

565
37:37.694 --> 37:39.362
Hey, Mi-do, are you okay? Are you hurt?

566
37:39.488 --> 37:40.822
[sighs deeply]

567
37:41.490 --> 37:42.824
I saw you grabbing Mi-do.

568
37:42.949 --> 37:44.076
What the hell, scumbag?

569
37:44.701 --> 37:45.660
Fucking prick.

570
37:46.119 --> 37:48.246
-Why did you lay your hands on her? -[Wan-do] Yeong!

571
37:48.371 --> 37:49.539
[footsteps approaching rapidly]

572
37:49.790 --> 37:51.041
What are you doing?

573
37:51.166 --> 37:52.334
Let go of him. What is this?

574
37:52.459 --> 37:53.627
Are you okay, Mi-do?

575
37:53.752 --> 37:55.420
[Yeong-do] Hey, Mi-do, tell me, who's this asshole?

576
37:55.545 --> 37:56.588
I said that's enough!

577
37:56.713 --> 37:57.964
[Namgung] He was in the army with me.

578
38:02.886 --> 38:04.346
[heartfelt music continues]

579
38:17.943 --> 38:18.819
Are you okay?

580
38:21.446 --> 38:22.781
Are you hurt anywhere else?

581
38:28.537 --> 38:29.371
Hey, Mi-do.

582
38:35.001 --> 38:36.253
I was really scared.

583
38:39.506 --> 38:41.133
You took ten years off my life.

584
38:58.608 --> 38:59.860
[heartfelt music concludes]

585
39:00.777 --> 39:01.903
[groans softly]

586
39:10.829 --> 39:12.747
What the hell is going on today?

587
39:13.957 --> 39:15.959
I think you got the wrong idea here.

588
39:17.711 --> 39:18.879
Miss Lee and I…

589
39:20.505 --> 39:21.673
don't have anything.

590
39:24.217 --> 39:26.803
I just liked her, so I started following her around.

591
39:28.388 --> 39:29.681
She wasn't interested.

592
39:32.017 --> 39:33.059
I mean it.

593
39:42.569 --> 39:43.403
Not buying it?

594
39:43.987 --> 39:46.948
You didn't even try to fool me, just spouting nonsense.

595
39:47.866 --> 39:49.075
Wow.

596
39:50.327 --> 39:51.286
Clever.

597
39:51.620 --> 39:53.371
Do you have any idea what you did wrong?

598
39:54.623 --> 39:55.457
So many things.

599
39:56.499 --> 39:57.542
[grunts softly]

600
39:57.667 --> 39:58.668
What do you know?

601
40:00.420 --> 40:02.339
[Namgung] I know exactly one thing for sure.

602
40:03.173 --> 40:05.717
Mi-do got hurt, and you're just fine.

603
40:07.761 --> 40:10.055
What were you doing while her arm got crushed?

604
40:10.972 --> 40:13.225
You couldn't even protect her at all.

605
40:16.353 --> 40:17.938
Stay away from Mi-do, you hear?

606
40:19.648 --> 40:20.732
Or you'll regret it.

607
40:54.099 --> 40:55.392
I had my reasons.

608
40:58.478 --> 41:00.772
I know everything I say will sound as an excuse.

609
41:00.897 --> 41:03.817
[Namgung] Just tell me how miserable you actually want to make me.

610
41:07.487 --> 41:09.281
Do you have any idea what you've done?

611
41:12.951 --> 41:15.870
You turned all our time together into a complete waste.

612
41:18.748 --> 41:20.166
So you had your reasons.

613
41:21.710 --> 41:22.919
You had no other choice.

614
41:24.921 --> 41:26.715
You don't know why you did it either?

615
41:28.425 --> 41:29.843
Just be honest for once.

616
41:30.719 --> 41:35.056
You didn't give a damn if I got hurt, whether it affected me or not,

617
41:35.849 --> 41:38.101
or if our time ended up in the trash!

618
41:39.102 --> 41:41.980
You just selfishly did whatever the hell you wanted!

619
41:50.947 --> 41:52.657
Is that what you really think?

620
41:56.578 --> 41:57.662
Do you really think…

621
42:00.332 --> 42:02.000
it didn't matter if you got hurt?

622
42:04.002 --> 42:06.087
Or if all our time together was ruined,

623
42:06.796 --> 42:08.715
that I ignored all of that and thought only of myself?

624
42:08.840 --> 42:09.674
Am I wrong?

625
42:09.799 --> 42:10.633
You are.

626
42:11.301 --> 42:12.218
Yes, you are.

627
42:13.636 --> 42:15.430
It was agonizing for me too.

628
42:18.516 --> 42:20.101
You're everything to me, Namgung.

629
42:21.603 --> 42:23.813
You're still the most precious person in my life.

630
42:25.398 --> 42:28.651
I could never hurt you, not after everything you've been through.

631
42:29.194 --> 42:30.862
I've tried so hard to hide it from you.

632
42:31.404 --> 42:33.698
That made me hate myself even more than I already did.

633
42:34.282 --> 42:36.951
Actually, I fought so hard to hide it from myself.

634
42:37.202 --> 42:39.996
Do you have any idea how all your words sound to me?

635
42:40.705 --> 42:43.333
I was so crazy about him, I couldn't hold back.

636
42:43.458 --> 42:45.335
You meant nothing! That's the only thing I'm hearing!

637
42:45.460 --> 42:46.378
I know!

638
42:46.503 --> 42:47.420
I had a crush!

639
42:47.545 --> 42:48.505
I was flustered!

640
42:52.884 --> 42:54.219
[somber music playing]

641
42:54.344 --> 42:55.512
[exhales deeply]

642
42:55.637 --> 42:57.514
Every day was the same routine.

643
42:58.223 --> 43:00.266
Movies stopped being fun a while ago.

644
43:01.309 --> 43:04.604
I had no hope for my future, and I'm getting older.

645
43:05.647 --> 43:08.525
And so I thought to myself, oh…

646
43:10.485 --> 43:13.488
I'm just going to keep going like this until I'm old.

647
43:20.078 --> 43:21.996
And then my heart fluttered.

648
43:27.335 --> 43:31.423
If I say I felt like he suddenly lit up my bleak, dark life,

649
43:33.007 --> 43:34.801
would you believe it?

650
43:44.602 --> 43:45.437
No.

651
43:50.024 --> 43:52.110
It's just a pathetic excuse to justify it.

652
43:52.235 --> 43:53.278
That's all it is.

653
43:54.154 --> 43:56.281
I'm sure sugarcoating it makes you feel good.

654
44:01.744 --> 44:02.787
The thing is…

655
44:06.499 --> 44:09.085
I feel I'm being punished whenever you act like this.

656
44:11.337 --> 44:13.465
We never should have dated in the first place.

657
44:15.633 --> 44:20.763
Before we ruin each other even more, let's get out of each other's lives, yeah?

658
44:21.473 --> 44:23.099
[music rises]

659
44:38.781 --> 44:40.200
[sniffles]

660
44:45.872 --> 44:48.583
[sobbing softly]

661
44:51.753 --> 44:53.004
[exhales deeply]

662
44:53.129 --> 44:54.214
[somber music concludes]

663
44:56.758 --> 45:02.013
[phone alarm ringing]

664
45:09.354 --> 45:10.396
[phone alarm stops]

665
45:36.714 --> 45:39.384
[soft, sentimental music playing]

666
46:39.360 --> 46:40.403
-[phone alarm ringing] -[gasps]

667
46:40.528 --> 46:41.571
[shatters]

668
46:41.696 --> 46:43.114
[soft, sentimental music concludes]

669
46:43.239 --> 46:46.576
[phone alarm continues ringing]

670
46:51.664 --> 46:53.291
-[phone vibrates] -What's this?

671
46:53.416 --> 46:55.585
-Did you see the notice just now? -[phone vibrates]

672
46:55.710 --> 46:56.544
[gasps]

673
46:56.669 --> 47:00.089
[presenter] …powdered milk at 19%, and raw sugar at 16%.

674
47:00.214 --> 47:02.592
-Raw material prices are soaring… -[woman 1 gasping]

675
47:02.717 --> 47:04.052
[tense music playing]

676
47:07.889 --> 47:09.432
[exhales shakily]

677
47:10.808 --> 47:12.185
MANAGER EOM HO-SIK

678
47:20.068 --> 47:21.152
DISCIPLINARY NOTICE

679
47:21.277 --> 47:24.197
SUBJECT NAMGUNG HO IS HEREBY SUSPENDED FOR ONE WEEK

680
47:26.574 --> 47:28.284
[gasps] Namgung Ho?

681
47:28.409 --> 47:29.577
That assistant manager?

682
47:29.702 --> 47:31.704
[woman 2] There's a lot of talk about loan sharks.

683
47:31.829 --> 47:33.039
He must have taken a bribe.

684
47:33.164 --> 47:37.418
Didn't he fix that outsourcing rate with their CEO behind the scenes?

685
47:37.543 --> 47:41.047
[panting]

686
47:49.430 --> 47:50.431
[GPS tracker beeps]

687
47:51.265 --> 47:52.558
[Su-a] By the Dongbo Pharma billboard.

688
47:52.684 --> 47:54.394
There's a field and a drain, am I right?

689
47:54.519 --> 47:56.604
Hey, tell me, you dumped them there?

690
47:59.607 --> 48:00.441
[gasps]

691
48:00.566 --> 48:03.152
[determined music playing]

692
48:07.740 --> 48:10.326
TO: ACE Q-LAB FOOD ANALYSIS INSTITUTE

693
48:20.753 --> 48:21.879
[determined music fades]

694
48:22.004 --> 48:23.506
Still slippery on the left side.

695
48:23.631 --> 48:25.007
[panting]

696
48:25.133 --> 48:26.217
This is all my fault.

697
48:28.261 --> 48:30.471
I put a GPS on Mr. Oh's truck last week.

698
48:30.888 --> 48:32.473
I think that's what went wrong.

699
48:34.308 --> 48:35.268
The thing is…

700
48:36.602 --> 48:38.146
I tried to be really careful.

701
48:38.896 --> 48:41.524
I used five VPNs to hide my identity.

702
48:42.150 --> 48:43.818
And I only paid with crypto.

703
48:44.777 --> 48:46.404
Even if the GPS was discovered…

704
48:46.529 --> 48:48.656
[panting]

705
48:51.492 --> 48:52.326
It can't be.

706
48:52.452 --> 48:53.578
Any sweet potatoes left?

707
48:53.703 --> 48:55.329
There's no way you could have used them all.

708
48:56.330 --> 48:58.499
Uh… Mr. Namgung took them this morning.

709
48:59.208 --> 49:00.168
[gasps softly]

710
49:03.254 --> 49:04.672
That's what you keep saying.

711
49:08.176 --> 49:09.427
It was a trap from the start.

712
49:10.928 --> 49:14.140
The sweet potatoes from Cheonan Factory was a trap all along.

713
49:15.516 --> 49:17.143
The texture got too crunchy.

714
49:19.145 --> 49:21.022
I told them to make it denser.

715
49:21.147 --> 49:23.691
Man, the frozen department is lazy with the desserts.

716
49:25.610 --> 49:28.696
You did it intentionally, didn't you?

717
49:29.113 --> 49:31.032
You knew it was a trap and you went for it.

718
49:32.784 --> 49:33.993
It's not that serious.

719
49:34.827 --> 49:36.204
At worst, the team disbands,

720
49:36.537 --> 49:38.748
I get a pay cut and sent to a factory.

721
49:40.041 --> 49:42.084
Maybe a transfer to another department.

722
49:42.210 --> 49:43.044
You know why?

723
49:43.461 --> 49:44.837
Because I'm completely clean.

724
49:46.964 --> 49:47.799
Su-a.

725
49:48.549 --> 49:50.134
Now is not the time to zone out.

726
49:51.093 --> 49:52.220
Pull yourself together.

727
49:52.845 --> 49:54.639
If they think it's me and drop their guard,

728
49:54.764 --> 49:56.098
you can investigate.

729
49:58.017 --> 50:00.228
And you need to investigate to settle this.

730
50:03.272 --> 50:04.398
[sighs]

731
50:04.524 --> 50:06.067
So I can come back to the team.

732
50:07.151 --> 50:08.236
But this still isn't right.

733
50:08.611 --> 50:09.737
I'll say what I know.

734
50:09.862 --> 50:12.031
[Namgung] Then this whole thing gets buried forever.

735
50:15.201 --> 50:16.828
I'm not gonna dig deeper.

736
50:17.537 --> 50:19.163
[gentle music playing]

737
50:22.250 --> 50:23.334
So you do it.

738
50:25.503 --> 50:26.671
Only you can investigate.

739
50:30.049 --> 50:31.676
Why'd you change your mind so suddenly?

740
50:31.801 --> 50:33.427
You didn't want me doing this.

741
50:36.138 --> 50:37.223
That was a lie.

742
50:39.475 --> 50:41.143
I really thought you were impressive.

743
50:43.855 --> 50:45.606
I thought you were amazing, actually.

744
50:48.693 --> 50:49.944
So you should keep going.

745
50:51.320 --> 50:52.363
Do what's right.

746
51:04.041 --> 51:05.209
[gentle music concludes]

747
51:05.334 --> 51:07.712
-[phones ringing] -[man whispering] That's him.

748
51:07.837 --> 51:12.258
[employees whispering indistinctly]

749
51:13.885 --> 51:16.304
[whispering rises]

750
51:18.598 --> 51:19.515
Hey, sir.

751
51:20.933 --> 51:22.685
Your phone keeps ringing.

752
51:25.521 --> 51:26.564
45 MISSED CALLS FROM YEONG-DO

753
51:26.689 --> 51:28.816
-[phone vibrates] -[Sang-hun] I wasn't snooping or anything.

754
51:28.941 --> 51:30.401
I checked just in case.

755
51:32.069 --> 51:33.321
YEONG-DO

756
51:33.446 --> 51:34.280
[Yeong-do] What is this?

757
51:34.739 --> 51:36.365
Namgung, did you know about this?

758
51:36.490 --> 51:37.366
[heavy music playing]

759
51:37.491 --> 51:41.662
DIRECTOR LEE MI-DO QUITS SONG HAE-NA FILM REPLACED BY DIRECTOR NA SEUNG-HO

760
51:44.540 --> 51:45.666
[heavy music concludes]

761
51:46.250 --> 51:47.293
[sighs]

762
51:47.418 --> 51:49.962
[voicemail] The person you are trying to reach is unavailable

763
51:50.087 --> 51:51.255
at the tone…

764
51:51.756 --> 51:52.715
Still no word from her?

765
51:53.466 --> 51:55.343
She's not answering her phone. What do we do?

766
51:55.468 --> 51:56.594
[sighs]

767
51:57.303 --> 51:58.971
She always hides when there's trouble.

768
51:59.096 --> 52:00.222
Every freaking time!

769
52:01.223 --> 52:03.434
How many times did I say she was going to fail?

770
52:04.185 --> 52:06.562
She should have quit when her film tanked five years ago!

771
52:07.271 --> 52:08.606
That brat would be better off doing hair.

772
52:09.106 --> 52:10.816
I'm going to make her quit drinking for good.

773
52:11.776 --> 52:14.487
Why did she even try to make movies in the first place?

774
52:14.612 --> 52:15.613
I don't get it.

775
52:16.072 --> 52:16.906
Yeong.

776
52:17.573 --> 52:18.741
Yeah, I'm really sorry.

777
52:19.450 --> 52:20.701
I can barely even look at your face.

778
52:21.327 --> 52:23.913
When she gets back here, I'm going to chew that brat out

779
52:24.163 --> 52:25.873
for losing her mind and wasting her youth.

780
52:26.540 --> 52:27.792
I'll knock some sense into her.

781
52:28.417 --> 52:29.418
Shut your mouth.

782
52:33.422 --> 52:36.342
If you ever talk like that in front of Mi-do…

783
52:37.718 --> 52:39.220
I won't overlook that.

784
52:40.262 --> 52:41.514
You'd be dead to me.

785
52:45.685 --> 52:47.186
Mi-do is the most affected by this.

786
52:47.979 --> 52:49.605
What do you even know about her struggle?

787
52:53.651 --> 52:54.485
Guys.

788
52:55.486 --> 52:56.445
[exhales sharply]

789
52:58.864 --> 52:59.991
[sighs]

790
53:01.993 --> 53:06.247
Ms. Ma, I know you're disappointed in your daughter.

791
53:09.041 --> 53:10.668
But I know she gave it her all.

792
53:12.628 --> 53:18.551
If you see her, please just pretend this didn't happen, or she'll fall apart.

793
53:21.429 --> 53:22.513
I'm begging you.

794
53:33.524 --> 53:34.692
I'll call you when I find her.

795
53:42.033 --> 53:44.452
[door chime tinkles]

796
53:46.579 --> 53:48.664
[emotional music playing]

797
54:04.638 --> 54:05.639
[barista] Welcome, sir.

798
54:08.309 --> 54:09.351
[sighs]

799
54:15.399 --> 54:16.233
MIDORI

800
54:18.903 --> 54:21.697
[voicemail] The person you're trying to reach is unavailable.

801
54:22.865 --> 54:23.991
[Namgung sighs]

802
54:35.961 --> 54:37.713
Stay away from Mi-do, you hear?

803
54:37.963 --> 54:39.256
Or you'll regret it.

804
54:40.132 --> 54:41.717
[Tae-seung] And what about you, huh?

805
54:44.428 --> 54:45.554
What did you do for her?

806
54:45.679 --> 54:46.639
[sighs]

807
54:49.725 --> 54:51.936
You have no idea why she was in that accident.

808
54:53.312 --> 54:55.815
You wouldn't talk like that if you knew.

809
54:56.065 --> 54:57.066
[music rises]

810
54:57.191 --> 54:58.651
You better watch your damn mouth.

811
54:59.443 --> 55:01.112
There's only so much I can take.

812
55:04.657 --> 55:06.200
You really have no idea.

813
55:09.036 --> 55:11.205
Do you think Mi-do only shattered her arm?

814
55:13.457 --> 55:14.416
That's not all.

815
55:15.751 --> 55:17.419
She's broken on the inside.

816
55:28.305 --> 55:31.308
[man] Uh, we've acquired the dashcam footage from the vehicle

817
55:31.433 --> 55:32.685
that hit Han Tae-seung.

818
55:33.394 --> 55:37.231
It's a bit sensitive, but please, check the video first.

819
55:54.874 --> 56:00.963
[car horns honking]

820
56:16.812 --> 56:18.397
[emotional music concludes]

821
56:23.444 --> 56:25.487
[ambient music playing over speakers]

822
56:28.449 --> 56:29.575
[sighs]

823
56:35.497 --> 56:37.082
[Namgung] When did it all start?

824
56:38.209 --> 56:40.252
Mi-do slowly withering away.

825
56:41.629 --> 56:45.966
Namgung, is it really okay if my movie flops?

826
56:47.384 --> 56:50.554
You said it didn't matter if my movie flopped.

827
56:51.680 --> 56:53.098
I'm terrible, aren't I?

828
56:53.224 --> 56:55.226
[passionate Korean pop song playing]

829
56:55.351 --> 56:56.310
I disappointed you.

830
56:59.521 --> 57:02.483
[car horn honking]

831
57:02.608 --> 57:03.442
[Namgung] Mi-do was…

832
57:07.363 --> 57:10.574
without a doubt, the brightest person I ever knew.

833
57:20.376 --> 57:22.211
[song swells]

834
57:31.428 --> 57:35.891
[Namgung] She was always the main character of this whole story.

835
57:36.016 --> 57:38.102
[principal] In recognition of outstanding achievement

836
57:38.227 --> 57:41.438
at the Seoul Youth Film Festival hosted by the Garam Foundation,

837
57:41.563 --> 57:42.815
we hereby present this award.

838
57:42.940 --> 57:43.774
[classmates applauding]

839
57:49.113 --> 57:50.823
YEONUL HIGH SCHOOL 2009 YOUTH FILM FESTIVAL

840
57:50.948 --> 57:52.574
GRAND PRIZE LEE MI-DO, YEONUL HIGH SCHOOL

841
57:55.786 --> 57:57.413
[classmates cheering]

842
58:07.339 --> 58:10.884
[Namgung] Every person I knew had love for you.

843
58:24.148 --> 58:27.693
Your dreams made me feel butterflies.

844
58:28.569 --> 58:32.323
And I couldn't help but love you even more for it.

845
59:04.813 --> 59:07.024
YEONUL ELEMENTARY SCHOOL

846
59:11.070 --> 59:13.238
-[passionate Korean pop song concludes] -[panting]

847
59:22.623 --> 59:23.624
[exhales deeply]

848
59:38.722 --> 59:39.556
You know,

849
59:41.600 --> 59:42.643
when I was young,

850
59:45.354 --> 59:47.606
I never once imagined that I'd…

851
59:49.775 --> 59:51.860
end up being a pathetic adult.

852
59:53.862 --> 59:54.780
Huh…

853
59:55.155 --> 59:59.118
I was crazy. So young and arrogant.

854
01:00:02.788 --> 01:00:04.623
But the more humiliating thing

855
01:00:06.625 --> 01:00:09.002
is the side of me you're seeing right now.

856
01:00:11.004 --> 01:00:14.591
I only ever wanted to show you the best side of me.

857
01:00:16.427 --> 01:00:18.929
And I always ended up showing you the worst.

858
01:00:21.807 --> 01:00:23.016
That's something I hate.

859
01:00:46.957 --> 01:00:48.208
[heartfelt music playing]

860
01:00:52.087 --> 01:00:53.630
[Namgung] Your hands are really cold.

861
01:00:56.091 --> 01:00:57.593
You need to go home.

862
01:01:12.441 --> 01:01:14.485
Don't you hate me even a little?

863
01:01:17.321 --> 01:01:19.281
After how I treated you?

864
01:01:21.200 --> 01:01:24.536
Why don't you… What?

865
01:01:28.707 --> 01:01:29.708
Mi-do…

866
01:01:33.670 --> 01:01:35.964
I want you to listen to me very carefully.

867
01:01:38.175 --> 01:01:40.052
I haven't lost my mind at all,

868
01:01:41.637 --> 01:01:43.555
and I'm dead serious about this.

869
01:01:54.107 --> 01:01:55.484
Please go see that guy.

870
01:01:55.609 --> 01:01:56.944
[heartfelt music concludes]

871
01:02:01.490 --> 01:02:02.574
[Namgung] That guy…

872
01:02:06.203 --> 01:02:08.080
who lit up your bleak, dark life.

873
01:02:13.085 --> 01:02:14.253
Go see him now.

874
01:02:18.757 --> 01:02:21.677
["Stay" playing]

875
01:02:40.195 --> 01:02:42.072
A LOVE OTHER THAN YOURS

876
01:02:57.546 --> 01:02:59.590
[Dong-hwan] Even if we put him on the anchovy boat?

877
01:02:59.923 --> 01:03:00.757
He's relentless.

878
01:03:01.216 --> 01:03:02.801
[Yeon-ho] We need someone to get samples.

879
01:03:02.926 --> 01:03:05.345
[Mi-do] You know that Su-a has feelings for you.

880
01:03:05.721 --> 01:03:08.223
[Namgung] Should I just accept being dragged around by you?

881
01:03:08.890 --> 01:03:11.018
Living in fear of being discarded?

882
01:03:11.435 --> 01:03:12.477
You should have flat-out denied it.

883
01:03:12.603 --> 01:03:14.104
Why haven't you done that?

884
01:03:14.229 --> 01:03:15.480
There's nothing happening between us.

885
01:03:16.398 --> 01:03:17.733
He doesn't even know that I like him.

886
01:03:18.984 --> 01:03:19.818
[Mi-do] Then you do it too.

887
01:03:20.611 --> 01:03:22.112
You see other women as well.

888
01:03:23.780 --> 01:03:25.741
Subtitle translation by Soya Back (백소야)

889
01:03:26.074 --> 01:03:26.992
[song concludes]
